---
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import photo from "../assets/gabriel.jpg";
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="About · ceifa"
  description="Gabriel Francisco, ceifa on the internet. Software developer from Belo Horizonte, Brazil."
>
  <div class="about-page">
    <section class="page-head">
      <h1><span data-land="text" id="first-perch">Hi, I'm Gabriel.</span></h1>
    </section>
    <figure class="portrait">
      <Image
        src={photo}
        alt="Gabriel smiling, in a red t-shirt."
        width={200}
        height={200}
        densities={[1, 2]}
        loading="eager"
        data-land="top"
      />
      <figcaption>Me, not the duck.</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <div class="about-body">
      <p>
        <span data-land="text"
          >I'm a software developer in Belo Horizonte, Brazil, and these days a CTO. I'm 1.92 m tall,
          my desktop runs CachyOS (so yes, technically I use Arch) and I'll take a regular Coke over a
          Zero every single time.</span
        >
      </p>
      <p>
        <span data-land="text"
          >Most of my life lives in a git repository. Bills, trips, doctor's appointments, the people
          I know: it's all markdown, kept up to date by an AI agent called Mortar. Mortar books my
          appointments, plans our trips and, with my blessing, answers satisfaction surveys for me. If
          you ever sent me an NPS survey, there's a good chance Mortar is the one who answered.</span
        >
      </p>
      <p>
        <span data-land="text"
          >Away from the keyboard I'm usually on the road with my girlfriend. So far that's been the
          dunes of Jalapão, Iguaçu Falls, Porto Seguro and Florianópolis, and the US is next. Back
          home I host a modded Minecraft server for us and our friends, and a script claims my free
          Brawl Stars gift every day before I can forget.</span
        >
      </p>
      <p>
        <span data-land="text"
          >One more thing you'd find out eventually: I don't wear plastic. No polyester, no nylon, no
          elastane, not even 5% of it. I read the label of every shirt before it gets near me.</span
        >
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
